1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,427
Book Three, Proposition Nine.

2
00:00:02,427 --> 00:00:12,741
If a point be taken within a circle, and more than two equal segments fall from the point on the circle, the point taken is the center of the circle.

3
00:00:12,741 --> 00:00:22,640
Let A B C be a circle and D a point within it, and from D let more than two equal segments, namely D A, D B, and D C, fall on the circle A B C.

4
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:26,170
I say that the point D is the center of the circle.

5
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:34,237
Join the chords A B and B C by Postulate One, and bisect them at the points E and F by One Ten.

6
00:00:34,237 --> 00:00:41,160
Then join E D and F D, and extend them across the circle to the points G, K, H, and L.

7
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:50,426
Because A E equals E B, E D is common, and base D A equals base D B, the triangles A E D and B E D are congruent by One Eight.

8
00:00:50,426 --> 00:00:59,694
Therefore angle A E D equals angle B E D, so each is a right angle by Definition Ten, and G K bisects the chord A B at right angles.

9
00:00:59,694 --> 00:01:10,015
By the Porism to Three One, the perpendicular bisector of any chord passes through the center of the circle; hence the center of A B C lies on G K.

10
00:01:10,015 --> 00:01:14,929
By the exact same reasoning on chord B C, the center also lies on H L.

11
00:01:14,929 --> 00:01:23,425
Since the two straight lines G K and H L have no point in common except D, the point D is the center of the circle A B C.

12
00:01:23,425 --> 00:01:25,180
As was required to prove.

13
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:40,253
Already cited by Aristotle in the Meteorologica, Proposition Three Nine is the logical contrapositive of Three Seven: since no eccentric point can send three equal segments to a circle, any point that does must be the center.

14
00:01:40,253 --> 00:01:57,120
Rather than relying on indirect proof from Three Seven as Simson later did, Heiberg's critical edition preserves Euclid's direct constructive proof—intersecting two perpendicular chord bisectors from Three One across thirty-four ancestor nodes in the G-Index.

15
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:11,525
